  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:100729",
  "description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: proc: protect ptrace_may_access() with exec_update_lock (FD links) (CVE-2026-64375)\n  * kernel: Bluetooth: bpa10x: avoid OOB read of revision string in bpa10x_setup() (CVE-2026-64549)\n  * kernel: wifi: mwifiex: bound uAP association event IEs to the event buffer (CVE-2026-68326)\n  * kernel: wifi: mac80211: validate extension-frame layout before RX (CVE-2026-68470)\n  * kernel: net/smc: fix socket use-after-free during link group termination (CVE-2026-74493)\n  * kernel: wifi: mwifiex: use the subframe length when parsing A-MSDU TDLS frames (CVE-2026-74488)\n  * kernel: net: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice (CVE-2026-74631)\n  * kernel: perf/core: Fix group leader use-after-free after sibling detach (CVE-2026-74637)\n  * kernel: nvdimm/btt: reject an arena whose nfree is below the lane count (CVE-2026-89965)\n  * kernel: slip: remove slip_hangup() to fix use-after-free in slip_receive_buf() (CVE-2026-90057)\n  * kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Unlink NVMe unsol ctx before freeing on LS reject error (CVE-2026-97528)\n  * kernel: RDMA/siw: Bound fragmented header copies by the remaining length (CVE-2026-98323)\n  * kernel: cipso: adjust cached option offsets when removing CIPSO (CVE-2026-99064)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * [AlmaLinux-8] The slab cache entries for gfs2 and dlm grow very large for gfs2 filesystems (JIRA:RHEL-220529)\n  * XFS NULL pointer dereference in xfs_inode_mark_reclaimable due to race in xfs_free_perag during umount (JIRA:RHEL-247835)\n  * kprobe/ftrace: use-after-free and panic after ftrace_kill(), needs backport of 1a7d0890dd4a and e113f0b46d19 (JIRA:RHEL-284885)\n  * Critical Bug Fixes for customer issues with lpfc [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:RHEL-286158)\n  * Backport CVEs from v7.2 [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:RHEL-300371)\n  * Fix crasher in gss_unwrap_resp_integ() (JIRA:RHEL-309171)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
